Why do we need interface 

consider this example 

import javax.swing.plaf.ComboBoxUI;

class Developer 
{
  public void develop(Computer comp) // we stricly set that class Developer onlu develope with laptop, and this actually the problem of tight 
                                     // coupling , we only dependent on Laptop. we need more higly level, to add also Desktop and Computer 
  {
    comp.dev();
  }
}

class Laptop implements Computer
{
  public void dev()
  {
    System.out.println("Developing with laptop");
  }
}

// but what if we can give not only the laptop, but also Desktop

class Desktop implements Computer
{
  public void dev()
  {
    System.out.println("Developing with desktop ");
  }
}

// the solution is interface 
interface Computer 
{
  void dev();
}

class Main
{
  public static void main()
  {
    Developer AKs = new Developer();

    Computer lap = new Laptop();
    AKs.develop(lap);
  }
}

